<title>INDIA: Indian soybean plants stay shut against taxes.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean plants stay shut against taxes.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean processing plants in central India remained shut for the 16th day due to protests against trade taxes, dealers said.</p>
<p>The central state of Madhya Pradesh which accounts for 80 percent of India's soybean production doubled the market tax to two percent and imposed other levies on May 1.</p>
<p>The processing industry immediately went on strike alongwith the trade.</p>
<p>--Bombay newsroom +91-22-265-9000</p>
